            <ArticleTitle>Left ventricular ballooning syndrome due to vasospasm of the middle portion of the left anterior descending coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>314-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case that shows vasospasm to be one of the mechanisms responsible for left ventricular ballooning syndrome. Our case suggests that identical ventriculographic findings in patients with tako-tsubo syndrome and those with coronary vasospasm of a long left anterior descending artery coronary artery may be due to a common etiology.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
